# Cloudflare Pages headers.

# The board is gated by Cloudflare Access, which already keeps crawlers out - they never
# get past the login. These headers are the second layer, for the case where Access is
# ever misconfigured, disabled, or bypassed: even then, a crawler that reaches the page is
# told not to index it, not to follow out of it, and not to keep a cached copy.
# noarchive matters most here. Without it a search engine can serve a cached snapshot of
# the page long after the page itself is locked down again.
/to-do-items/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive, nosnippet
  Cache-Control: private, no-store, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
